(3588517, 502103, 76184, '<td valign="top">lots of noise, and camera shake.<br/>Next time, I''d suggest turning down the ISO to eliminate noise, and using a tripod with the camera on a 2 second delay. That way your hands will be off the camera when the shutter opens and closes.<br/> <br/>If you have the camera set on S or A, it tries to resolve any dark areas with detail that you may not be able to pull. Use the lowest ISO setting you can, and use the manual setting. This will go a long way to reducing the amount of noise you get.</td>', 'lots of noise, and camera shake.Next time, I''d suggest turning down the ISO to eliminate noise, and using a tripod with the camera on a 2 second delay. That way your hands will be off the camera when the shutter opens and closes. If you have the camera set on S or A, it tries to resolve any dark areas with detail that you may not be able to pull. Use the lowest ISO setting you can, and use the manual setting. This will go a long way to reducing the amount of noise you get.', '2007-04-27 15:22:30.000000', NULL, 1),
