(3610910, 502349, 68256, '<td valign="top">Thanks!  It took f22 to get the whole flower in focus!  I appreciate all of your comments.</td>', 'Thanks!  It took f22 to get the whole flower in focus!  I appreciate all of your comments.', '2007-05-03 15:05:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611117, 501174, 62095, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot with good thumbnail appeal.  I think with a bit more sharpness (contrast?) it would have scored up in the sixes.</td>', 'This is a great shot with good thumbnail appeal.  I think with a bit more sharpness (contrast?) it would have scored up in the sixes.', '2007-05-03 15:59:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611121, 502051, 62095, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, postcard-like quality to it, I think.</td>', 'Nice shot, postcard-like quality to it, I think.', '2007-05-03 16:00:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611332, 502669, 30982, '<td valign="top">Positives - I quite like the boldness of it.  This probably is also a negative in DPC-land, where harsh light/shadows are not our friends in many instances.  Heck with it - I like sunlight and lots of it.<br/> <br/>Technicals - See above about sunlight, promptly ignore as you see fit.  Good detail in the leaves themselves.  Noticeable lack of "jaggies" despite the very sharp edges of the leaves, too.<br/> <br/>Meets challenge - Yep.  Though somehow I''m betting the anal retentive among us felt the subject took up too much of the frame.<br/> <br/>Distractions/point removers:  The one partial leaf at the top intrudes without contributing, in my opinion.  And the subject matter itself is probably not "wow" enough to garner higher votes.</td>', 'Positives - I quite like the boldness of it.  This probably is also a negative in DPC-land, where harsh light/shadows are not our friends in many instances.  Heck with it - I like sunlight and lots of it. Technicals - See above about sunlight, promptly ignore as you see fit.  Good detail in the leaves themselves.  Noticeable lack of "jaggies" despite the very sharp edges of the leaves, too. Meets challenge - Yep.  Though somehow I''m betting the anal retentive among us felt the subject took up too much of the frame. Distractions/point removers:  The one partial leaf at the top intrudes without contributing, in my opinion.  And the subject matter itself is probably not "wow" enough to garner higher votes.', '2007-05-03 17:03:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611514, 502241, 30982, '<td valign="top">Not only did you get a 6, but you got a perfect 6.0000.  That''s pretty nifty!  What I like about this is the quiet relationship between the two crossed flowers, the lovely little white ones below, and the "neighborhood gossip" flower in the background keeping such a close eye on the other two.</td>', 'Not only did you get a 6, but you got a perfect 6.0000.  That''s pretty nifty!  What I like about this is the quiet relationship between the two crossed flowers, the lovely little white ones below, and the "neighborhood gossip" flower in the background keeping such a close eye on the other two.', '2007-05-03 17:37:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611515, 502241, 67152, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6 during voting.  The bokeh in the background is really  nice and smooth.  The interlocking flowers has a really sweet and gentle quality about it and the intersection of the two stems is really nicely placed at the upper third.  The colors are really rich and deep - especially the golden hues of the flower.  I think a little more separation of light between the subjects in focus and the background would really make this one stand out much more.  Nice work.</td>', 'I gave this a 6 during voting.  The bokeh in the background is really  nice and smooth.  The interlocking flowers has a really sweet and gentle quality about it and the intersection of the two stems is really nicely placed at the upper third.  The colors are really rich and deep - especially the golden hues of the flower.  I think a little more separation of light between the subjects in focus and the background would really make this one stand out much more.  Nice work.', '2007-05-03 17:38:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611558, 502241, 52439, '<td valign="top">I love it personally. <br/>It''s one of very few photos that just looks ''real'', like a i could reach into the photo and touch the flower.<br/>I would of given this an 8.</td>', 'I love it personally. It''s one of very few photos that just looks ''real'', like a i could reach into the photo and touch the flower.I would of given this an 8.', '2007-05-03 17:48:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611568, 502241, 53316, '<td valign="top">Oh gosh, such awesome colors!! I love them. I also like the interesting "tilting" feeling that the background has.</td>', 'Oh gosh, such awesome colors!! I love them. I also like the interesting "tilting" feeling that the background has.', '2007-05-03 17:50:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611619, 502478, 52713, '<td valign="top">What a great shot! Just where do you get that lens???? ;-)<br/> <br/>Congrats on your new PB!</td>', 'What a great shot! Just where do you get that lens???? ;-) Congrats on your new PB!', '2007-05-03 18:00:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611780, 502051, 66384, '<td valign="top">Congratulation on the 6+ score. I think the light is beautiful in this shot. There must be some tall trees or large buildings off to the right of the shot, because I don''t understand the shadows -- they don''t seem to be cast by the barn. Great contrast, and good use of rule of thirds.</td>', 'Congratulation on the 6+ score. I think the light is beautiful in this shot. There must be some tall trees or large buildings off to the right of the shot, because I don''t understand the shadows -- they don''t seem to be cast by the barn. Great contrast, and good use of rule of thirds.', '2007-05-03 18:43:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611798, 501880, 66384, '<td valign="top">Wow, 6.4+, congratulations. I got a laugh from your comment that it was taken in the McDonalds parking lot. It''s so lovely and wild looking -- definitely looks like a beach local. Beautiful sky and good example of rule of thirds.</td>', 'Wow, 6.4+, congratulations. I got a laugh from your comment that it was taken in the McDonalds parking lot. It''s so lovely and wild looking -- definitely looks like a beach local. Beautiful sky and good example of rule of thirds.', '2007-05-03 18:50:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611817, 502173, 66384, '<td valign="top">Deb, I like the image: the colors, patterns, contrast. My eye doesn''t find anything to rest on, though. It seems to lack a focal point.</td>', 'Deb, I like the image: the colors, patterns, contrast. My eye doesn''t find anything to rest on, though. It seems to lack a focal point.', '2007-05-03 18:59:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3611888, 502241, 45475, '<td valign="top">It''s a technically sound image. The exposure''s good, the dof is superb (bit of bokeh going on there, magic) and that''s why you got the well deserved high marks. But at the end of the day, it''s just a flower shot. For flower shots to evoke lots of response, they need to pack a punch. Either with in-your-face dramatic/mother-of-all bright colour, or with exquisite (perfectly executed) shallow dof/macro. It needs a little something more to grab the viewer''s attention and compel them to tell you that they''ve been absolutely spellbound by your imagery and want to have your baby.</td>', 'It''s a technically sound image. The exposure''s good, the dof is superb (bit of bokeh going on there, magic) and that''s why you got the well deserved high marks. But at the end of the day, it''s just a flower shot. For flower shots to evoke lots of response, they need to pack a punch. Either with in-your-face dramatic/mother-of-all bright colour, or with exquisite (perfectly executed) shallow dof/macro. It needs a little something more to grab the viewer''s attention and compel them to tell you that they''ve been absolutely spellbound by your imagery and want to have your baby.', '2007-05-03 19:25:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612100, 502015, 64994, '<td valign="top">Killer shot! I love sunsets/sunrises and this a GREAT one.</td>', 'Killer shot! I love sunsets/sunrises and this a GREAT one.', '2007-05-03 20:40:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612110, 500718, 64994, '<td valign="top">Nice angle and I love the shadows, very cool light effect as well!</td>', 'Nice angle and I love the shadows, very cool light effect as well!', '2007-05-03 20:43:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612147, 501551, 45115, '<td valign="top">one of the best nudes I''ve seen on this website so far.</td>', 'one of the best nudes I''ve seen on this website so far.', '2007-05-03 20:56:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612158, 501135, 67697, '<td valign="top">I love deer but they are so hard to capture.  It''s a great closeup and I love all the background colors.</td>', 'I love deer but they are so hard to capture.  It''s a great closeup and I love all the background colors.', '2007-05-03 20:58:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612222, 500310, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very pretty.  I love the early light shining on the rocks and the trees.  The cool white tones of the water help bring out the goose a little bit too.  Nice!</td>', 'Very pretty.  I love the early light shining on the rocks and the trees.  The cool white tones of the water help bring out the goose a little bit too.  Nice!', '2007-05-03 21:17:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612267, 502600, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is very pretty.  I love the chain going into the red and coming out thru the blue.  The detail on the wall is excellent and I love the sky reflection in the water.</td>', 'This is very pretty.  I love the chain going into the red and coming out thru the blue.  The detail on the wall is excellent and I love the sky reflection in the water.', '2007-05-03 21:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612274, 502573, 67697, '<td valign="top">And he doesn''t look very happy to have that bird resting on his head, does he.  This is a hilarious capture. Too bad the right side was cut off a bit.</td>', 'And he doesn''t look very happy to have that bird resting on his head, does he.  This is a hilarious capture. Too bad the right side was cut off a bit.', '2007-05-03 21:32:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612279, 502386, 67697, '<td valign="top">That''s too bad you were sick - hope you are feeling better now!  I love the light coming thru the window.  The color tones and grains give it that nice old-time feel.</td>', 'That''s too bad you were sick - hope you are feeling better now!  I love the light coming thru the window.  The color tones and grains give it that nice old-time feel.', '2007-05-03 21:33:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612284, 502173, 67697, '<td valign="top">You have so many interesting things to photograph!  I like the silhouettes.  This turned out very well considering it looks like it must have been pretty bright outside.</td>', 'You have so many interesting things to photograph!  I like the silhouettes.  This turned out very well considering it looks like it must have been pretty bright outside.', '2007-05-03 21:35:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612285, 501961, 67697, '<td valign="top">A very nice and simple shot.  What a beautiful bird!  Love the contrast of the subject with the beautiful sky.</td>', 'A very nice and simple shot.  What a beautiful bird!  Love the contrast of the subject with the beautiful sky.', '2007-05-03 21:36:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612289, 500773, 67697, '<td valign="top">You always have such nice photos.  I love the sharpness, detail, and contrast of this pic.   The patterns and lines lead you into the depth of the photo.  This is great!</td>', 'You always have such nice photos.  I love the sharpness, detail, and contrast of this pic.   The patterns and lines lead you into the depth of the photo.  This is great!', '2007-05-03 21:37:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612466, 501161, 62318, '<td valign="top">Zero comments, that''s a shame. <br/> <br/>Voters are fickle... sometimes they like negative space sometimes they don''t. Tough scene to capture since the action is so small, however I like the intent... stark red against the blue sky.<br/> <br/>One mantra my professor always stated, "Fill the Frame". I think if you would have cut this into a portrait orientation you would have had a much stronger photo. Though, take my ramblings lightly, my average is lower than yours. :)<br/> <br/>As far as pure technicals, the image is nearly perfect.</td>', 'Zero comments, that''s a shame.  Voters are fickle... sometimes they like negative space sometimes they don''t. Tough scene to capture since the action is so small, however I like the intent... stark red against the blue sky. One mantra my professor always stated, "Fill the Frame". I think if you would have cut this into a portrait orientation you would have had a much stronger photo. Though, take my ramblings lightly, my average is lower than yours. :) As far as pure technicals, the image is nearly perfect.', '2007-05-03 22:07:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612695, 502550, 67697, '<td valign="top">I like the composition of the tree and the blue sky.  The lighting on the flowers in the foreground is awesome!</td>', 'I like the composition of the tree and the blue sky.  The lighting on the flowers in the foreground is awesome!', '2007-05-03 22:53:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612714, 502263, 67697, '<td valign="top">What''d ya do to the grass?  It looks pretty cool.  The zebra has a lovely glow about it as well.</td>', 'What''d ya do to the grass?  It looks pretty cool.  The zebra has a lovely glow about it as well.', '2007-05-03 23:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612735, 501128, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very nice contrast with the red against the blue and white background.  A very striking image!</td>', 'Very nice contrast with the red against the blue and white background.  A very striking image!', '2007-05-03 23:08:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612742, 501525, 67697, '<td valign="top">Aww you captured true, natural bonding.  They look so much alike with the white patches on their heads.  Interesting choice in using black and white.</td>', 'Aww you captured true, natural bonding.  They look so much alike with the white patches on their heads.  Interesting choice in using black and white.', '2007-05-03 23:11:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612758, 502459, 67697, '<td valign="top">Meowch you got some happy comments lol.  Contre-jour, yeah probably.  I like the starburst - I don''t know how to do that.  I think something that would have been interesting to try is to have used the flash at the same time to highlight what looks to me like flowers in the foreground on the left.  I don''t know if that would work or not lol.</td>', 'Meowch you got some happy comments lol.  Contre-jour, yeah probably.  I like the starburst - I don''t know how to do that.  I think something that would have been interesting to try is to have used the flash at the same time to highlight what looks to me like flowers in the foreground on the left.  I don''t know if that would work or not lol.', '2007-05-03 23:14:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3612799, 502449, 31307, '<td valign="top">Hoowah!  Chalk up another one.</td>', 'Hoowah!  Chalk up another one.', '2007-05-03 23:27:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3613386, 501551, 76184, '<td valign="top">Thank you, Toyan. I appreciate, that.</td>', 'Thank you, Toyan. I appreciate, that.', '2007-05-04 02:11:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3613430, 501026, 76184, '<td valign="top">Two people have called this a B&amp;W photo. I think some of y''all need to adjust your monitors...or I do. There is plenty of color here. It is a desaturated shot, but the color hasn''t been totally removed.</td>', 'Two people have called this a B&W photo. I think some of y''all need to adjust your monitors...or I do. There is plenty of color here. It is a desaturated shot, but the color hasn''t been totally removed.', '2007-05-04 02:29:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3613434, 500241, 76184, '<td valign="top">While I like cats, I loathe cat photos...<br/> <br/>I gave this one a 7. I''m glad to see it did well. You composed this well, and managed some great colors.</td>', 'While I like cats, I loathe cat photos... I gave this one a 7. I''m glad to see it did well. You composed this well, and managed some great colors.', '2007-05-04 02:31:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3613449, 502449, 6870, '<td valign="top">Well done, Zoom!</td>', 'Well done, Zoom!', '2007-05-04 02:36:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3613511, 502616, 30982, '<td valign="top">Amazing shot!  Love the mercury-like quality of the water''s surface and the indents from the feet.  Great capture very well presented.</td>', 'Amazing shot!  Love the mercury-like quality of the water''s surface and the indents from the feet.  Great capture very well presented.', '2007-05-04 03:04:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3613571, 499850, 37252, '<td valign="top">Amazing capture - excellent DOF, and composition. Congrats!</td>', 'Amazing capture - excellent DOF, and composition. Congrats!', '2007-05-04 03:57:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(3613946, 502013, 8367, '<td valign="top">Wow! What a rush! Congratulations. An amazing capture. <br/>Did anyone take any photos of you in the Decathlon RV4?<br/></td>', 'Wow! What a rush! Congratulations. An amazing capture. Did anyone take any photos of you in the Decathlon RV4?', '2007-05-04 08:58:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614109, 502049, 45549, '<td valign="top">Gia kapoion logo, molis eida thn fwto hmou sxedon sigouros oti htan dikh sas (-:<br/> <br/>Aperanto galazio....poly omorfh.</td>', 'Gia kapoion logo, molis eida thn fwto hmou sxedon sigouros oti htan dikh sas (-: Aperanto galazio....poly omorfh.', '2007-05-04 09:56:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614114, 501845, 8367, '<td valign="top">One of my top rated. Great timing to capture this perfect composition for rule of thirds.</td>', 'One of my top rated. Great timing to capture this perfect composition for rule of thirds.', '2007-05-04 09:58:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614365, 502693, 64707, '<td valign="top">It reminds me of moonlight shots in the older movies.  I really like it very much.</td>', 'It reminds me of moonlight shots in the older movies.  I really like it very much.', '2007-05-04 10:50:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614549, 502013, 33542, '<td valign="top">I love this picture, although the spacing feels a little off - like there''s no real way to make this fit the rule of thirds. It seems a little too close to the center the way it is because the wings are so much bigger than the body, but if it were farther towards the edge I don''t think it would have looked right either. May have been better as a freestudy entry, but congrats on the top 10 anyway! It''s a great shot, rule of thirds or not.</td>', 'I love this picture, although the spacing feels a little off - like there''s no real way to make this fit the rule of thirds. It seems a little too close to the center the way it is because the wings are so much bigger than the body, but if it were farther towards the edge I don''t think it would have looked right either. May have been better as a freestudy entry, but congrats on the top 10 anyway! It''s a great shot, rule of thirds or not.', '2007-05-04 11:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614594, 502449, 70299, '<td valign="top">Wow...nice Rule of Thirds.  Whitworth College is my AlmaMater...class of ''92!  I love seeing anything you have from Spokane!  And I can''t wait to visit there again, someday.  congratulations on the ribbon!</td>', 'Wow...nice Rule of Thirds.  Whitworth College is my AlmaMater...class of ''92!  I love seeing anything you have from Spokane!  And I can''t wait to visit there again, someday.  congratulations on the ribbon!', '2007-05-04 12:00:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614755, 501008, 61651, '<td valign="top">I had to look at this one for a while - it does look like a window pane.  Nice sly wink at all those voters with their rulers out, QED indeed! :)</td>', 'I had to look at this one for a while - it does look like a window pane.  Nice sly wink at all those voters with their rulers out, QED indeed! :)', '2007-05-04 12:36:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614760, 501161, 61651, '<td valign="top">Cool play of tones in all the blues and greens here.</td>', 'Cool play of tones in all the blues and greens here.', '2007-05-04 12:38:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614768, 501525, 61651, '<td valign="top">This expresses such a nice mood of tenderness - color version I think would not have been as effective for evoking that mood.</td>', 'This expresses such a nice mood of tenderness - color version I think would not have been as effective for evoking that mood.', '2007-05-04 12:40:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614803, 501961, 61651, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a new personal best - a nice quiet, simple capture.</td>', 'Congrats on a new personal best - a nice quiet, simple capture.', '2007-05-04 12:56:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614807, 502573, 61651, '<td valign="top">Good eye for an amusing shot - he just doesn''t look too happy, does he?</td>', 'Good eye for an amusing shot - he just doesn''t look too happy, does he?', '2007-05-04 12:57:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614837, 501532, 57032, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>This is a great shot. It is well framed, and certainly meets this challenge. I''m very impressed that you were able to freeze the moon so well, especially with such a wide angle lens (it can be difficult to focus when the moon takes up so little of the frame). Colour is good and exposure is perfect, with the pitch black background providing a great backdrop for the subject. Sharpness is good, with no haloes or obvious signs of PP. This is a magnificent crop--just a great job of using the tools you have available to pull off what for many would turn out to be a pixel-ridden or grainy result.<br/> <br/>As many have already said, I too am surprised this scored as low as it did.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Geoff Ball</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club, This is a great shot. It is well framed, and certainly meets this challenge. I''m very impressed that you were able to freeze the moon so well, especially with such a wide angle lens (it can be difficult to focus when the moon takes up so little of the frame). Colour is good and exposure is perfect, with the pitch black background providing a great backdrop for the subject. Sharpness is good, with no haloes or obvious signs of PP. This is a magnificent crop--just a great job of using the tools you have available to pull off what for many would turn out to be a pixel-ridden or grainy result. As many have already said, I too am surprised this scored as low as it did. Regards,Geoff Ball', '2007-05-04 13:13:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614844, 502600, 61651, '<td valign="top">Cool take on thirds - I think this would look interesting completely flipped the other way up, too.</td>', 'Cool take on thirds - I think this would look interesting completely flipped the other way up, too.', '2007-05-04 13:18:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614860, 502173, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nice slice of life shot, good silhouettes.  Curious about those numbers in the windows - I wonder what they are for (general question, not "why do you have them in the shot")?</td>', 'Nice slice of life shot, good silhouettes.  Curious about those numbers in the windows - I wonder what they are for (general question, not "why do you have them in the shot")?', '2007-05-04 13:21:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614865, 502386, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nice natural light and graininess.  I like "quiet" images like this.</td>', 'Nice natural light and graininess.  I like "quiet" images like this.', '2007-05-04 13:22:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614866, 501313, 61651, '<td valign="top">The swirly bokeh is fabulous, and such a great expression on the duck - this is very nice.  I had given it an 8.</td>', 'The swirly bokeh is fabulous, and such a great expression on the duck - this is very nice.  I had given it an 8.', '2007-05-04 13:23:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614868, 502646, 61651, '<td valign="top">Very nice color contrasts.</td>', 'Very nice color contrasts.', '2007-05-04 13:24:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614874, 500451, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nice positioning in the frame, I like how we "peek through" the branches at the bird.  The bird looks a bit either overexposed or over sharpened - honestly I can''t tell which - but what can you do?</td>', 'Nice positioning in the frame, I like how we "peek through" the branches at the bird.  The bird looks a bit either overexposed or over sharpened - honestly I can''t tell which - but what can you do?', '2007-05-04 13:26:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614879, 500653, 61651, '<td valign="top">This has a nice private moment feel to it - great range of understated colors in the background.</td>', 'This has a nice private moment feel to it - great range of understated colors in the background.', '2007-05-04 13:28:09.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3614881, 502015, 61651, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your fantastic score - nice application of thirds here.</td>', 'Congrats on your fantastic score - nice application of thirds here.', '2007-05-04 13:29:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614884, 500718, 61651, '<td valign="top">Basking - that ''s the word I think of when looking at this - just "basking". [hint: that''s a compliment] :)</td>', 'Basking - that ''s the word I think of when looking at this - just "basking". [hint: that''s a compliment] :)', '2007-05-04 13:30:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614886, 501532, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nicely done - have not been successful myself yet in getting a moon shot like this.</td>', 'Nicely done - have not been successful myself yet in getting a moon shot like this.', '2007-05-04 13:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3614890, 502550, 61651, '<td valign="top">I like the selective focus on this and how the background flora has this impressionistic wash look to it.</td>', 'I like the selective focus on this and how the background flora has this impressionistic wash look to it.', '2007-05-04 13:32:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615075, 501453, 30982, '<td valign="top">Initial reaction - a conversation.  That''s what I see, is a conversation between these two old friends of the evening sky.  <br/> <br/>Technicals - very good job getting both the moon and star relatively crisp given that the moon moves WAY faster than most people think.<br/> <br/>Meets challenge - Ah, here''s the rub - seems many of the voters wanted Rule of Thirds to have a subject exactly at one of the four intersections of the grid.  I suspect many used grids when voting, too.  I of course see this as meeting rule of thirds by having three distinct "boxes" in the photograph, but I''m weird.<br/> <br/>Are you happy with it?  Did you achieve what you set out to do?  Then it be good!</td>', 'Initial reaction - a conversation.  That''s what I see, is a conversation between these two old friends of the evening sky.   Technicals - very good job getting both the moon and star relatively crisp given that the moon moves WAY faster than most people think. Meets challenge - Ah, here''s the rub - seems many of the voters wanted Rule of Thirds to have a subject exactly at one of the four intersections of the grid.  I suspect many used grids when voting, too.  I of course see this as meeting rule of thirds by having three distinct "boxes" in the photograph, but I''m weird. Are you happy with it?  Did you achieve what you set out to do?  Then it be good!', '2007-05-04 14:34:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615078, 502058, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Wow, if I had voted on this Challenge, you would have had at least one more high score.  So that shows my bias in this critique.  I like it; nice work.<br/> <br/>However, and with the caveat that I realize you have done a way-down closeup on this, it looks on my monitor as if it was over-sharp.  Whether this is the action of your macro set-up or post processing, it could give that impression to an average viewer.  <br/> <br/>And, yes, it could use just a touch less light on that green leaf.  The leaf appears a little ''hot''.  <br/> <br/>Still, in my book, nice shot.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Wow, if I had voted on this Challenge, you would have had at least one more high score.  So that shows my bias in this critique.  I like it; nice work. However, and with the caveat that I realize you have done a way-down closeup on this, it looks on my monitor as if it was over-sharp.  Whether this is the action of your macro set-up or post processing, it could give that impression to an average viewer.   And, yes, it could use just a touch less light on that green leaf.  The leaf appears a little ''hot''.   Still, in my book, nice shot.', '2007-05-04 14:35:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615102, 500651, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>You''ve done a beautifully moody image here.  It fits the Challenge perfectly, tells a good story, and is nicely photographed, especially under the Basic Rules.  <br/> <br/>You''ve placed quite well in a large field of entries.  Anything over 6 is pretty good pickings.  <br/> <br/>One of the problems with a "dark" image is that some of our voters do not have perfectly calibrated monitors and I think this may well have worked against this fine image.  If they could not see the subtle detail - which most certainly is there - they are going to vote low numbers.  <br/> <br/>While that''s the nature of the beast, it does not detract from the excellence of your work.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  You''ve done a beautifully moody image here.  It fits the Challenge perfectly, tells a good story, and is nicely photographed, especially under the Basic Rules.   You''ve placed quite well in a large field of entries.  Anything over 6 is pretty good pickings.   One of the problems with a "dark" image is that some of our voters do not have perfectly calibrated monitors and I think this may well have worked against this fine image.  If they could not see the subtle detail - which most certainly is there - they are going to vote low numbers.   While that''s the nature of the beast, it does not detract from the excellence of your work.', '2007-05-04 14:42:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615163, 501161, 74979, '<td valign="top">Nice Shot, Julie..AND a new Personal Best (the NC ribbon) to boot!  Good for you!  Now I have a new goal!  Take care~</td>', 'Nice Shot, Julie..AND a new Personal Best (the NC ribbon) to boot!  Good for you!  Now I have a new goal!  Take care~', '2007-05-04 14:56:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615172, 501337, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial reaction - the first thing is of course the very strong face in the foreground, but it''s the secondary that catches my eye - what''s going on beyond?  What''s real, what isn''t?  It creates a very intriguing tension within the shot.  The face in the foreground maintains control, however, constantly bringing you back.<br/> <br/>Technicals are strong - good light, good conversion, great detail in the foreground subject.  Appears to have met the challenge by voter standards.  Lack of significant number of comments indicates to me that most voters felt it was a very good photograph - not requiring a lot of "fix this" comments or garnering a lot of "WOW" comments either.  Very nice work.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial reaction - the first thing is of course the very strong face in the foreground, but it''s the secondary that catches my eye - what''s going on beyond?  What''s real, what isn''t?  It creates a very intriguing tension within the shot.  The face in the foreground maintains control, however, constantly bringing you back. Technicals are strong - good light, good conversion, great detail in the foreground subject.  Appears to have met the challenge by voter standards.  Lack of significant number of comments indicates to me that most voters felt it was a very good photograph - not requiring a lot of "fix this" comments or garnering a lot of "WOW" comments either.  Very nice work.', '2007-05-04 14:58:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615174, 502049, 74979, '<td valign="top">I thought this might be you during the challenge-lovey Greece!  You do love the ocean-eh?  Me too!</td>', 'I thought this might be you during the challenge-lovey Greece!  You do love the ocean-eh?  Me too!', '2007-05-04 14:58:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615194, 500801, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial reaction:  I like power lines.  I know that''s a strange reaction, but so many people seem intent on editing them out, and yet here you feature them prominently - I like that.  Seems to speak of the power of man, the power of nature.<br/> <br/>Technicals:  Perhaps a little soft but when dealing with the aforementioned powerlines, it''s indeed very difficult to sharpen without making the lines go all jaggy.  Lovely light and color, but the border seems just a tad heavy for the shot.  Either white, or a thinner black might be more balanced.<br/> <br/>Meets challenge - yep, sure does!<br/> <br/>Very good score and placement in this one, too.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial reaction:  I like power lines.  I know that''s a strange reaction, but so many people seem intent on editing them out, and yet here you feature them prominently - I like that.  Seems to speak of the power of man, the power of nature. Technicals:  Perhaps a little soft but when dealing with the aforementioned powerlines, it''s indeed very difficult to sharpen without making the lines go all jaggy.  Lovely light and color, but the border seems just a tad heavy for the shot.  Either white, or a thinner black might be more balanced. Meets challenge - yep, sure does! Very good score and placement in this one, too.', '2007-05-04 15:06:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615683, 502231, 72581, '<td valign="top">Thank You everyone! this is my best photo yet and was surprised at how well it did. Thanks to everyone who rated or commented it. Specail thanks to admart01 who helped me a lot with this picture.</td>', 'Thank You everyone! this is my best photo yet and was surprised at how well it did. Thanks to everyone who rated or commented it. Specail thanks to admart01 who helped me a lot with this picture.', '2007-05-04 17:32:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615773, 502626, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi there from the Critique Club</b> <br/>While 6 is a strong and very respectable score, I think this one is much stronger than a 6.0.  Technically and compositionally, you achieved a terrific capture here.  I absolutely love you depth of field use, and I think that it is the main strength of the image.  This is not to say that other areas of the image are lacking, though.  The color is wonderful, and the bokeh-esque green background does a great job setting off the brilliant yellow of the subject.  The focus is very nice, especially the very crisp droplets on the flower.  I believe that your scored suffered from commonality and nothing else.  The image is strong, but many voters simply tire of flowers.  While flowers are not one of my pet peeves, I can relate to the voters.  I tire of house cats, woodies and any shot that has the aurora borealis in it.  Often shots of common subjects lose points no matter the strength of the image.  I believe that happened to this one.  15 votes of 4 or less says it all.  Great image and a terrific addition to your front page.  <br/> <br/>Thanks for the opportunity to critique your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b></td>', 'Hi there from the Critique Club While 6 is a strong and very respectable score, I think this one is much stronger than a 6.0.  Technically and compositionally, you achieved a terrific capture here.  I absolutely love you depth of field use, and I think that it is the main strength of the image.  This is not to say that other areas of the image are lacking, though.  The color is wonderful, and the bokeh-esque green background does a great job setting off the brilliant yellow of the subject.  The focus is very nice, especially the very crisp droplets on the flower.  I believe that your scored suffered from commonality and nothing else.  The image is strong, but many voters simply tire of flowers.  While flowers are not one of my pet peeves, I can relate to the voters.  I tire of house cats, woodies and any shot that has the aurora borealis in it.  Often shots of common subjects lose points no matter the strength of the image.  I believe that happened to this one.  15 votes of 4 or less says it all.  Great image and a terrific addition to your front page.   Thanks for the opportunity to critique your entry,Eric', '2007-05-04 18:17:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3615905, 501400, 55956, '<td valign="top"><b>Greeting from critique club.</b> <br/> <br/>Hi, I agree with the Larus comment when he say that the duck is a bit to close in the corner. The image haven''t strong impact because the duck isn'' t very sharp. the most great problem of this photo is that it haven''t the wow effect. I think that the final rating is adapted.<br/> <br/>For any question send me a private message.<br/>Best regards <br/>Gennaro<br/></td>', 'Greeting from critique club.  Hi, I agree with the Larus comment when he say that the duck is a bit to close in the corner. The image haven''t strong impact because the duck isn'' t very sharp. the most great problem of this photo is that it haven''t the wow effect. I think that the final rating is adapted. For any question send me a private message.Best regards Gennaro', '2007-05-04 18:58:43.000000', NULL, 0),
